// version 9.0.0
// Mixed trace - Classical CAN + CAN FD frames on the SAME bus/channel.
// This mirrors real-world captures where a CAN FD-capable channel still carries
// plain Classical CAN frames (backward compatibility), so per the ASC spec the
// two event formats appear side by side with NO shared prefix keyword:
//
//   Classical CAN Data  : <Time> <Channel> <ID> <Dir> d <DLC> <D0>...<D7> Length = <MessageDuration> BitCount = <MessageLength> ID = <IDnum>[x]
//   Classical CAN Remote: <Time> <Channel> <ID> <Dir> r <DLC> Length = <MessageDuration> BitCount = <MessageLength> ID = <IDnum>[x]
//   CAN FD              : <Time> CANFD <Channel> <Dir> <ID> <SymbolicName> <BRS> <ESI> <DLC> <DataLength> <D1>...<D64> <MessageDuration> <MessageLength> <Flags> <CRC> <BitTimingConfArb> <BitTimingConfData>
//
// => A parser MUST branch on whether token[1] (right after <Time>) is the
//    literal string "CANFD" or a channel number, BEFORE reading anything else.
